{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-009",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 9,
  "title": "Job 9",
  "display_title": "Job 9",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 9,
  "sortOrder": 18009,
  "verseCount": 35,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Then Job answered and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "I know it is so of a truth: but how should man be just with God?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "If he will contend with him, he cannot answer him one of a thousand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "He is wise in heart, and mighty in strength: who hath hardened himself against him, and hath prospered?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Which removeth the mountains, and they know not: which overturneth them in his anger.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Which shaketh the earth out of her place, and the pillars thereof tremble.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Which commandeth the sun, and it riseth not; and sealeth up the stars.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Which alone spreadeth out the heavens, and treadeth upon the waves of the sea.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Which maketh Arcturus, Orion, and Pleiades, and the chambers of the south.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Which doeth great things past finding out; yea, and wonders without number.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Lo, he goeth by me, and I see him not: he passeth on also, but I perceive him not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Behold, he taketh away, who can hinder him? who will say unto him, What doest thou?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "If God will not withdraw his anger, the proud helpers do stoop under him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "How much less shall I answer him, and choose out my words to reason with him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Whom, though I were righteous, yet would I not answer, but I would make supplication to my judge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "If I had called, and he had answered me; yet would I not believe that he had hearkened unto my voice.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "For he breaketh me with a tempest, and multiplieth my wounds without cause.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "He will not suffer me to take my breath, but filleth me with bitterness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "If I speak of strength, lo, he is strong: and if of judgment, who shall set me a time to plead?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "If I justify myself, mine own mouth shall condemn me: if I say, I am perfect, it shall also prove me perverse.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Though I were perfect, yet would I not know my soul: I would despise my life.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "This is one thing, therefore I said it, He destroyeth the perfect and the wicked.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "If the scourge slay suddenly, he will laugh at the trial of the innocent.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "The earth is given into the hand of the wicked: he covereth the faces of the judges thereof; if not, where, and who is he?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Now my days are swifter than a post: they flee away, they see no good.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "They are passed away as the swift ships: as the eagle that hasteth to the prey.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "If I say, I will forget my complaint, I will leave off my heaviness, and comfort myself:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "I am afraid of all my sorrows, I know that thou wilt not hold me innocent.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "If I be wicked, why then labour I in vain?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "If I wash myself with snow water, and make my hands never so clean;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "Yet shalt thou plunge me in the ditch, and mine own clothes shall abhor me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "For he is not a man, as I am, that I should answer him, and we should come together in judgment.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "Neither is there any daysman betwixt us, that might lay his hand upon us both.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "Let him take his rod away from me, and let not his fear terrify me:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:34"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-035",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 35,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:9:35",
      "numberLabel": "35",
      "text": "Then would I speak, and not fear him; but it is not so with me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 9:35",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:9:35"
      }
    }
  ],
